# Surfaces — border, radius, ink, gap (always on)

**Golden sentence:** Depth comes from **border + surface ladder**, not cast shadows. Every fill owns its ink and hairline. Bordered peer sections never kiss (≥8px). Content inside a rounded shell insets ≥ the radius.

---

## No box-shadow elevation

**Golden sentence:** Studio chrome and ideal-stack UI **do not use cast box-shadows** for depth. Separate surfaces with **border + surface ladder** (`bg-canvas` / `bg-surface` / `bg-surface-raised`). Floating menus, cards, tiles, and popovers stay flat.

| Do | Don't |
| --- | --- |
| Edge = `border` / ink hairline (`border-on-surface/14`, `border-border-bui`) | `shadow-sm` / `shadow-md` / `shadow-lg` / `shadow-xl` |
| Depth = next surface rung (`bg-surface-raised` over `bg-surface`) | Blur / soft drop shadows under cards, grids, menus |
| Focus / selected = `ring-*` or transparent-reserve border | Fake elevation with `hover:shadow-*` |
| Shared menus via `MENU_*` / `SELECT_MENU_*` (no shadow) | One-off `shadow-lg` on View / account / context menus |

**Forbidden (elevation class):** `shadow`, `shadow-sm|md|lg|xl|2xl`, custom `shadow-[0_12px_40px_…]`, `hover:shadow-md` drag lift.

```ts
// ✅ flat card / menu — border + raised fill
"rounded-2xl border border-on-surface/14 bg-surface-raised"
// ❌ elevation shadow
"… bg-surface-raised shadow-sm hover:shadow-md"
```

**Allowed (not elevation):** `ring-*` / `ring-inset` for focus/selection; `shadow-[0_0_0_Npx_…]` as a **ring substitute** (zero blur); `shadow-[inset_…]` hairline; design-token **atlas** preview tiles (docs only); true vendor bridges that already paint shadows (prefer strip when we own the surface).

Flat surfaces: `HOME_WIDGET_TILE*`, `MENU_PANEL_*`, `SELECT_MENU_*`, context menus, composer popovers, directory tiles / settings groups — all border + fill only.

