## Background ↔ text / hairline awareness

**Golden sentence:** Every fill owns its ink and hairline — borders and labels follow the surface hue; never leave cool slate edges or muddy ink on a tinted shell.

| # | Law | Fail if |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **Ink from background** — fg clears WCAG AA (~4.5) on its fill | Chip/label ink same family as muted fill (brown-on-brown) |
| 2 | **Hairlines share hue** — borders = ink mixed onto the surface (or `border-on-surface/N`) | Cool `#232830` / zinc borders on warm yellow/brown shells |
| 3 | **One edge** — composer / token cards use a **single** hairline | `border` + inset `ring` double edge (aliased muddy frame) |
| 4 | **Theme paint updates border** — soft/fill shell patches set `border.default` / `strong` with bg/fg | Soft shell only patches `bg`/`fg`; leftover slate borders |
| 5 | **Nest one step** — text/cards inside a painted shell use the next ladder step (solid token) | `bg-surface-muted/20` tool cards inside a `bg-surface-raised` bubble |

### Surface ladder (Studio `--as-color-bg-*` → Tailwind)

| Role | Token | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Page / recessed well | `bg-canvas` | Desk body, **inset** wells inside raised cards (tools, `<pre>`, thinking) |
| Panel / column | `bg-surface` | Chat column, window body |
| Lifted chrome | `bg-surface-raised` (`sidebar`) | Bubbles, popovers, rails |
| Soft inset / chips | `bg-surface-muted` (`muted`) | Context chips, inline `code`, option pills |

**Nesting rule:** parent already on a shell fill → child uses a **different** rung (`canvas` recessed or `muted` chip), **solid** — never `*/10`–`*/30` washes of the same rung. Floating menus lift (`raised`), they don't match the parent.

### Soft / fill shell

When writing `STUDIO_THEME_SOFT_SHELLS` / `fillShell`: set `bg` + `fg` + **`border`** together; dark hairline ≈ mix primary ink ~14% onto surface; `expandFillShellPatch` already derives ink + hairline — don't strip them; rely on the hue scale (canvas ≠ surface ≠ sidebar ≠ muted).

Pure helpers: `@glassbox-studio/studio-core` → `pickReadableInk`, `deriveHairlineBorder`, `meetsContrast`, `ensureReadableFg`, `buildShellHueBgPalette`.

