## Chrome section gap — never kiss

**Golden sentence:** Adjacent **bordered** chrome sections (fields, chips, cards, outlined controls) **never kiss** — leave at least **8px** between peers so outlines read as separate.

| Relationship | Min gap | Tailwind | Token (`space.*`) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Icon cluster / segmented guts (same control) | 4px | `gap-1` | `1` |
| **Peer bordered sections** (field cells, chips, inset panels in a row) | **8px** | `gap-2` | `2` |
| Distinct field groups / toolbar bands | 12–16px | `gap-3` / `gap-4` | `3` / `4` |

**Floor for peer sections = 8px.** Prefer 12–16px when outlines are thick or labels sit on the border — tight 8px still looks fused. Put gap on the **row/stack** (`flex` + `gap-*`, grid `gap-*`); Studio reuses `GAP_SECTION` / `GAP_SECTION_COMFORT`. Don't rely on negative margins to "tighten" bordered peers; don't invent one-off `gap-[3px]`.

---

## Rounded inset pad

**Golden sentence:** Content inside a **rounded** chrome shell must clear the corner arc — inset ≥ radius on every edge that meets the curve. Never flush a control (button, input, checkbox row) into a rounded border.

`rounded-xl` ≈ **12px** → Studio floor inset **`px-3.5` / `pb-3.5` (14px)**. Larger radius → bump pad with the shell.

| # | Law | Fail if |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **Inset ≥ radius** | Control paint meets the curved stroke |
| 2 | **No full-bleed actions in rounded groups** | `w-full` button as last child with `mt-*` only, no `mx`/`mb`/`footer` |
| 3 | **Last child owns bottom air** | Final row/fieldset/footer has ≥ `pb-3.5` (or group uses padded footer) |
| 4 | **Match gutters** | Horizontal pad matches sibling rows (`SETTINGS_ROW` / `SETTINGS_FIELD` = `px-3.5`) |
| 5 | **Nested radius** | Prefer inset square-ish / shared button radius **inside** pad — never child corners sitting on parent corners |

| Do | Don't |
| --- | --- |
| `SETTINGS_ROW` / `SETTINGS_FIELD` / `SETTINGS_GROUP_FOOTER` | Bare `<button class="w-full">` as last child of `SETTINGS_GROUP` |
| `SETTINGS_FIELDSET` with bottom inset when last in group | `fieldset` `p-0` ending flush on the arc |
| Inset primary actions: `SETTINGS_GROUP_FOOTER` + `SETTINGS_BTN*` | `DATA_GRID_BTN_PRIMARY` edge-to-edge under `overflow-hidden rounded-xl` |
| Title **inside** a group: `px-3.5 pt-3.5` (or row) | `SETTINGS_GROUP_LABEL` (`px-1`) used as in-card title |

Settings tokens: `SETTINGS_ROW` / `SETTINGS_FIELD` (`px-3.5 py-3`), `SETTINGS_GROUP_FOOTER` (`px-3.5 pb-3.5 pt-2`), `SETTINGS_NEST_BAND` (already `p-3.5`), `SETTINGS_CHECK_ROW` (last check block still needs group/fieldset bottom inset).

---

## Agent checklist (every surface edit)

- [ ] No new `shadow-sm|md|lg|xl` or cast `shadow-[…]` on product chrome — border + surface ladder only
- [ ] New chip/token/composer edge uses ink-relative border (or hue-matched token border)
- [ ] Nested content steps the ladder (solid) — no low-opacity same-hue wash
- [ ] No new `border` + inset `ring` double frames
- [ ] Bordered peers have ≥ `gap-2` (8px); comfort rows use `gap-3`/`gap-4`
- [ ] Rounded shell: horizontal inset ≥ radius; bottom inset on last content or dedicated footer; no full-bleed rounded child flush to parent curve

